A||||4||rogergarrison||Inside Rearview Mirror||||6||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||04-02-2001||05:56 PM||||I installed an inside mirror from a Cadillac in my car over the weekend. Hot and ground wire is all you need, fits stock mount on glass. Dims automaticly when a lite from behind you hits it, then goes back when lite has passed. You all know how low we are, everyone blinds us. Cost me $25<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||hugh||04-02-2001||09:19 PM||||great idea,what year and model did it come from?||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-02-2001||09:37 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>great idea,what year and model did it come from?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>mine came from a 92 STS, but im sure any will work. Some have a built in compass too, for you guys that get lost ez. You wont even need to add any wire, the connector is just inside the front edge of headliner. Pull out as much as you can and cut it off. I tied it in to the dome lite power. There are 3 wires, red is hot, black is ground, green - leave off (goes to a connector/sensor in transmssion so it wont dim when in reverse).  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||04-02-2001||09:51 PM||||You can also get one from a Bonnie or other GM full size from the 90's.  Thats what I did.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
